your heart, and lean not on your own understanding;","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":3,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":22,"source":"openbible","text":"in all your ways acknowledge Him, and He will make your paths straight.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":121,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"The LORD will watch over your coming and going, both now and forevermore.","from":2},{"book":"ZEC","chapter":2,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"For I will be a wall of fire around it, declares the LORD, and I will be the glory within it.’”","from":2},{"book":"PSA","chapter":118,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":15,"source":"openbible","text":"It is better to take refuge in the LORD than to trust in man.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"4-5":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H6128","lemma":"עֲקַלְקַל","tr":"a·qal·qal","gloss":"crooked","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H3826","lemma":"לִבָּה","tr":"lib·bah","gloss":"heart","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H6466","lemma":"פָּעַל","tr":"pa·al","gloss":"to work","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":57},{"base":"H0205","lemma":"אָ֫וֶן","tr":"a·ven","gloss":"evil: wickedness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":77},{"base":"H3190","lemma":"יָטַב","tr":"ya·tav","gloss":"be good","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":117},{"base":"H3477","lemma":"יָשָׁר","tr":"ya·shar","gloss":"upright","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":119},{"base":"H5186","lemma":"נָטָה","tr":"na·tah","gloss":"to stretch","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":214},{"base":"H7965","lemma":"שָׁלוֹם","tr":"sha·lom","gloss":"peace","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":237},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":538},{"base":"H0854","lemma":"אֵת","tr":"et","gloss":"with","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":929}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":59,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"The way of peace they have not known, and there is no justice in their tracks. They have turned them into crooked paths; no one who treads on them will know peace.","from":5},{"book":"PRO","chapter":2,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"whose paths are crooked and whose ways are devious.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":128,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"that you may see your childrenʼs children. Peace be upon Israel!","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":7,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"My shield is with God, who saves the upright in heart.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":40,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Blessed is the man who has made the LORD his trust, who has not turned to the proud, nor to those who lapse into falsehood.","from":5},{"book":"GAL","chapter":6,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Peace and mercy to all who walk by this rule, even to the Israel of God.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":84,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For the LORD God is a sun and a shield; the LORD gives grace and glory; He withholds no good thing from those who walk with integrity.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":101,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I will set no worthless thing before my eyes. I hate the work of those who fall away; it shall not cling to me.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}